\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Copy score at 100 and 1,000 exposures (means over seeds, sizes averaged; 95\% intervals; points offset for legibility). In (a), (c) and (d), colour shows history and line style presentation (solid: bursts; dashed: spaced). Nouns at 100 and 1,000 exposures are different nouns, all scored at the end of training; lines join conditions, not time points. (a) Stable-kind corpora, Experiment~3 (ten new seeds). (b) Control: copy score of redrawn, half-kept and changing-shape bursts against how often a burst sentence repeats the previous one's shape (dashed: 100 exposures; solid: 1,000), with changing-shape spaced nouns and fixed-shape bursts at 1,000 as dotted reference lines. (c) Single-history corpora, Experiment~3 (five seeds): all familiar nouns have changing shapes (orange) or all have fixed shapes (blue). (d) Shifting-kind corpora, Experiment~2 (exploratory). Solid grey line and band: unseen nouns; dashed line: unseen nouns with a typical embedding. Experiment~2's stable-kind results are in Figure~\ref {fig:a10}.}}{8}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:a11}{{3}{8}{Copy score at 100 and 1,000 exposures (means over seeds, sizes averaged; 95\% intervals; points offset for legibility). In (a), (c) and (d), colour shows history and line style presentation (solid: bursts; dashed: spaced). Nouns at 100 and 1,000 exposures are different nouns, all scored at the end of training; lines join conditions, not time points. (a) Stable-kind corpora, Experiment~3 (ten new seeds). (b) Control: copy score of redrawn, half-kept and changing-shape bursts against how often a burst sentence repeats the previous one's shape (dashed: 100 exposures; solid: 1,000), with changing-shape spaced nouns and fixed-shape bursts at 1,000 as dotted reference lines. (c) Single-history corpora, Experiment~3 (five seeds): all familiar nouns have changing shapes (orange) or all have fixed shapes (blue). (d) Shifting-kind corpora, Experiment~2 (exploratory). Solid grey line and band: unseen nouns; dashed line: unseen nouns with a typical embedding. Experiment~2's stable-kind results are in Figure~\ref {fig:a10}}{figure.3}{}}
